        "src": "../assets/toys/palm/thumb.webp",
        "alt": "The palm tree toy on the Splashery shelf"
      },
      "link": {
        "href": "../",
        "label": "Open the toy box"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "lookout",
      "title": "Lookout hill",
      "label": "Lookout",
      "at": [9.5, -7.5],
      "facing": 190,
      "words": "The whole island from its highest point. Near things are drawn with many small splats and far things with fewer, larger ones, so the view fits your device's splat budget. Try walking down the steep rocks to the west: the character stops where the slope is too steep."
    },
    {
      "id": "boulders",
      "title": "Boulder garden",
      "label": "Boulders",
      "at": [16.5, 12],
      "facing": 250,
      "words": "Boulders to walk around. Each has an invisible collider, so the character slides along it instead of walking through."
    },
    {
      "id": "lighthouse",
      "title": "The lighthouse",
      "label": "Lighthouse",
      "at": [-6, -21],
      "facing": 10,
      "words": "A big prop, still sharp from across the island. Worlds are made from a world file: its title, colors, terrain, props, landmarks and spawn point. The format is written up for anyone building a world.",
